From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Kholodnyi <andrei.kholodnyi@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] env hooks: skip library_path hook when cross-compiling

The library_path environment hook prepends a package's install lib dir to
LD_LIBRARY_PATH. colcon sources the install base when it assembles each
package's build command environment, so for a cross-build the VxWorks target
install lib dir (target .so files incl. libc.so.1) lands on the HOST
LD_LIBRARY_PATH during the build.

That entry is useless for a cross-build: the compiler/linker resolve target
libs via -L/-rpath-link (toolchain / cc-conf), and the target runtime loader
uses its own path config -- not the host LD_LIBRARY_PATH. But it breaks any
dynamically-linked HOST tool invoked during the build (ccache, cargo's host
build-script linker), whose loader picks a VxWorks soname and fails to start:

  <tool>: error while loading shared libraries: libc.so.1: cannot open shared object file

The hook is registered from several places (the ament_cmake_core default
descriptor, ament_export_libraries(), and directly from packages such as rclpy
and ros_workspace). Guard it once at the common chokepoint -- ament_environment_
hooks() -- so every emitter is covered: when CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING is set, skip
any hook named 'library_path'. CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING is TRUE whenever the
toolchain sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME (VxWorks), so native builds are unaffected.
---
 ament_cmake_core/cmake/environment_hooks/ament_environment_hooks.cmake | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ament_cmake_core/cmake/environment_hooks/ament_environment_hooks.cmake b/ament_cmake_core/cmake/environment_hooks/ament_environment_hooks.cmake
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/ament_cmake_core/cmake/environment_hooks/ament_environment_hooks.cmake
+++ b/ament_cmake_core/cmake/environment_hooks/ament_environment_hooks.cmake
@@ -38,6 +38,17 @@ function(ament_environment_hooks)
 
     get_filename_component(hook_filename "${hook}" NAME)
 
+    # VxWorks cross-build: skip the library_path hook. It prepends the install
+    # lib dir (target .so files) to LD_LIBRARY_PATH, which is useless for a
+    # cross-build (compiler/linker use -rpath-link; target loader uses its own
+    # path) and breaks dynamically-linked host tools (ccache, cargo host linker)
+    # invoked during the build. Single chokepoint for all emitters
+    # (ament_cmake_core default, ament_export_libraries, rclpy, ros_workspace).
+    get_filename_component(_hook_basename_check "${hook}" NAME_WE)
+    if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND _hook_basename_check STREQUAL "library_path")
+      continue()
+    endif()
+
     # check if the file is a template
     if(hook_filename MATCHES "^(.*)\\.in$")
       set(is_template TRUE)
